# Security Rules

- **Secrets** (API keys, DB credentials, signing keys) are only ever read from
  a secrets manager (e.g. Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager) or,
  locally, a git-ignored `.env` loaded by the typed config object
  (`000-general.mdc`). Never hardcode, never log, never put in a Docker
  `ARG`/`ENV` baked into an image layer.
- **Dependency hygiene**: lockfiles committed (`poetry.lock`/`package-lock.json`),
  automated vulnerability scanning in CI (`300-devops.mdc` stage 6), and a
  documented policy for how fast a critical CVE must be patched (e.g. 48h).
- **Least privilege everywhere**: cloud IAM roles scoped per-service, skill
  permissions scoped per-bot (`120-agent-safety.mdc`), DB users scoped to the
  schemas they need.
- **Input validation at every trust boundary**: API request bodies, tool
  outputs, file uploads, environment variables — validate with
  pydantic/zod before use, reject on mismatch rather than coercing silently.
- **Audit logging** for any action with real-world side effects (sending
  data externally, spending money, modifying persistent state) — who/what
  triggered it, what the inputs were, what the outcome was.
- **PII handling**: identify any field that can contain PII in the data
  model, document retention/redaction policy in `/docs/data-handling.md`,
  and ensure the observability redaction pass (`300-devops.mdc`) actually
  covers it — verify with a test, don't just assume the regex works.
